    "https://www.austincollege.edu/details/~board/jobs/post/assistant-professor-engineering": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Engineering | Details Skip To Main Content Toggle Close Container Close Menu Logo - Mobile Menu Utility Nav Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Apply Visit (opens in new window/tab) Give Campus Offices & Services News & Events Menu Layout Wrapper Menu Logo - Desktop LINKS FOR: New Students Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Cursive Text Expect the unexpected. Mobile  Kangoroo Image Search Search Clear Search Main Nav Academics Admission & Aid Campus Life Athletics (opens in new window/tab) Mobile Main Nav Academics Majors, Minors & Programs Student Success First-Year Experience Internships JanTerm Admission & Aid Visit (opens in new window/tab) Apply Scholarships Financial Aid Find Your Counselor Campus Life Wellness & Safety Living on Campus Dining Clubs & Greek Life Religious Life Athletics (opens in new window/tab) EXPLORE AUSTIN COLLEGE in words in NUMBERS in PICTURES in OUTCOMES ON A TOUR Menu Image Watermark Header Holder Header Logo Header Right Column Toggle Menu Container Menu Show Container Hovered Hovered Container Toggle Canvas Menu - Container Toggle Menu Canvas Utility Nav - Header Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Apply Visit (opens in new window/tab) Give Campus Offices & Services News & Events In this Section... Horizontal Nav Breadcrumb Assistant Professor of Engineering The Austin College Department of Physics and Engineering invites applications for the tenure-track position of Assistant Professor of Engineering. Candidates must have Ph.D. in hand before the position begins in August 2027. We encourage applications from candidates with enthusiasm for teaching and involving undergraduates in their research. Candidates with expertise in industrial engineering, manufacturing engineering, mechanical engineering or similar fields are particularly encouraged to apply. The department has six faculty members and is home to undergraduate degree programs in engineering, engineering physics, and physics. The Bachelor of Science in Engineering degree program was launched in Fall 2025 and is growing rapidly. Students may choose to complete a concentration in mechanical or electrical engineering, or graduate without a concentration. The successful candidate will support a variety of undergraduate engineering courses through all levels of the curriculum. The new faculty member will bring with them expertise that will help shape the continued growth of the program, including the potential addition of a third engineering concentration. In addition, the new faculty member will be an integral part of preparation for ABET accreditation, lab space setup, and establishment of the program’s culture. The department faculty are dedicated teacher-scholars with a strong commitment to teaching, undergraduate research, broad education, and mentoring in a liberal arts environment. We seek candidates who can engage students through hands-on learning and foster connections with regional industries. The College supports and encourages faculty-led research and scholarship through startup support, the Summer Sciences Research Program, and access to professional development funds. The successful candidate will also contribute to the Austin College Compass Curriculum by offering January Term courses every other year and participating in the First-Year Experience mentoring program. The program benefits from the strong growth of the semiconductor industry. Major companies are investing heavily in semiconductor fabrication facilities in Sherman TX, creating abundant opportunities for Austin College engineering students and faculty. This is enhanced by the College’s proximity to the Dallas-Fort Worth metroplex. The College is also a founding member of the Texoma Semiconductor Innovation Consortium recently designated a Tech Hub authorized by the CHIPS and Science Act. Austin College is a leading national private liberal arts college located north of Dallas in Sherman, Texas. Founded in 1849, it is the oldest institution of higher education in Texas operating under original charter and name. Recognized nationally for academic excellence in the areas of international education, pre-professional training, and leadership studies, the College provides an academically challenging and lively community of students, staff, and faculty committed to intellectual growth through individual and collaborative endeavors. Austin College (AC) is one of 40 schools profiled in Loren Pope’s influential book, Colleges That Change Lives . Candidates should send the following: letter of application CV copies of graduate transcripts (unofficial are sufficient for the application) statement of teaching philosophy, no more than one page statement of research, no more than one pages a statement reflecting on the composition of our student body and outlining how they would engage all our students in their teaching, scholarship, and/or service. Please combine materials into one PDF document and email it to our Engineering Search team . Three references should send recommendation letters directly to the aforementioned email address with the candidate’s name in the subject line. For full consideration, applications must be received by October 19, 2026 . Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. Austin College is an Equal Opportunity Employer that serves a diverse student body and is committed to the same in the hiring process. Faculty Positions Footer Holder Footer Logo Footer Address 900 N. Grand Avenue Sherman TX 75090 903-813-2000 Socials Facebook (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Quick Links Campus Conduct Hotline Mental Health Resources Human Resources Title IX Office Consumer Information Connect Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Subscribe (opens in new window/tab) Contact Us Directory Login Student Portal (opens in new window/tab)